{
  "requirement": "Start an agent request that will decode its submitted answer as `R`. Its graph tools share the dependency list used by direct reads under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.shared_context`.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D> {\n    pub fn ask<R>(&self) -> Ask<'_, 'd, D, R, ContextPhase>\n    where\n        R: DeserializeOwned + JsonSchema + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The text of `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.ask` has three obligations. `ask::<R>()` starts an agent request. The request decodes the submitted answer as `R`. Graph tools reached through that request record into the same dependency list as direct reads, which is the cited `shared_context`.\n\n- **Shared dependency list.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[verify_returns_direct_and_tool_reads_in_one_trace]` runs a criterion whose `execute` first calls `cx.read` on node 42 directly. It then calls `cx.ask::<bool>()`, and the scripted agent's `read_node` tool reads node 7. The test asserts that the returned answer's dependencies are exactly `[Node 42, Node 7]`, in that order. It also asserts that the backend served two calls. A separate dependency list for the agent's tools would fail this assertion.\n- **Decoding as `R`.** The same test submits `{\"result\": true}` and the criterion decodes it as `bool`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asks for `Answer` and asserts `answer.n == 7`. It also asserts that the schema sent to the agent has `properties.n.type == \"integer\"`, which shows the `JsonSchema` bound is used. The `assert_send(&future)` call covers the `Send` bound.\n- **Context dependency list across calls.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace]` interleaves direct reads with `ask` calls on the same context. It asserts the combined dependency order. It also asserts that a later `ask` leaves the existing trace unchanged.\n- **Signature.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public export inventory and that the Habeas consumer compiles against the SDK. That is adequate for the declared signature.\n\nI found no untested obligation, and every test has a `{test}` reference to the subject.",
